<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>app.curant.watcher</string>

    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <!-- Deliberately NOT /usr/bin/python3 (Apple's system Python).
             Same reasoning as com.curant.facetime.plist: this script
             uses osascript to drive Messages.app (see send_text_reply),
             which needs Automation/AppleEvents permission — macOS ties
             that grant to the exact requesting binary, not to whatever
             terminal/shell launched it. Using the same Homebrew
             python3.12 already granted permissions for the FaceTime
             answerer keeps both jobs consistent and avoids needing a
             second, separate grant for a different binary. -->
        <string>/opt/homebrew/opt/python@3.12/bin/python3.12</string>
        <!-- -u: unbuffered stdout/stderr — without it Python fully
             block-buffers output when not attached to a real terminal,
             so StandardOutPath/StandardErrorPath can sit empty for a
             long time even while the job is genuinely running. -->
        <string>-u</string>
        <string>/usr/local/bin/curant-watcher.py</string>
    </array>

    <key>RunAtLoad</key>
    <true/>

    <key>KeepAlive</key>
    <true/>

    <!-- launchd does not source .zshrc/.zprofile, so curant-cli
         (installed to this Mac's personal ~/bin, confirmed via `which
         curant-cli`) won't be found on the default PATH unless it's set
         explicitly here. Without /Users/AbhyudayDhundhel/bin
         specifically, every subprocess.run(["curant-cli", ...]) call —
         relay(), report-error, mark-job-delivered — fails outright with
         "No such file or directory", the same bug confirmed live on the
         FaceTime answerer's identical launchd setup. -->
    <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
    <dict>
        <key>PATH</key>
        <string>/Users/AbhyudayDhundhel/bin:/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin</string>
    </dict>

    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>/tmp/curant-watcher.log</string>

    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>/tmp/curant-watcher-error.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
<!--
Install with:
  cp curant-watcher.py /usr/local/bin/curant-watcher.py
  cp com.curant.watcher.plist ~/Library/LaunchAgents/
  launchctl bootout gui/$(id -u)/app.curant.watcher 2>/dev/null
  launchctl bootstrap gui/$(id -u) ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.curant.watcher.plist

Check it's running:
  launchctl print gui/$(id -u)/app.curant.watcher | grep -E "state|program|last exit"

Logs land at /tmp/curant-watcher.log and /tmp/curant-watcher-error.log
while testing — move these somewhere more permanent once stable.

Note: `launchctl load`/`unload` (the legacy API) can throw a generic
"Input/output error" on newer macOS even when nothing is actually
wrong — use `bootout`/`bootstrap` instead, which give real errors.
-->
